  "3|Emma Isshin Ashina Wolf Kuro Genichiro is a young doctor who saved her from a battlefield and was adopted by lord Dogen [1]. She started studying medicine from a young age to repay her master, becoming a skilled doctor fascinated by the white mark on Wolf's face [1]. Emma explains that unlike Wolf's resurrection power, Genichiro's derives from his consumption of the Rejuvenating Sediment [2].": false,
  "6|Prayer Beads are \"A loose prayer bead\" [1] that serve as an offering to increase maximum Vitality and Posture when given to a Sculptor's Idol. They can also be converted into a Prayer Bead Necklace, which further increases these same attributes. In total, there are 40 Prayer Beads in the game, though some may become unobtainable if specific charms like the Young Lord's Bell Charm are not acquired before defeating the Divine Dragon.": true,
  "8|Genichiro Ashina is a character and mandatory boss in which the player is meant to lose [1]. He is the current leader of the Ashina Clan, adopted after the death of his peasant mother [1]. Genichiro seeks to abduct Kuro and obtain the Divine Heir's gift of immortality to save both his beloved country and his clan [1].": true,
  "9|In the Shura ending, you must fight Emma, the Gentle Blade and Isshin Ashina back to back [1].": true,
  "11|In the Immortal Severance ending, Wolf must stab Kuro in the heart with the Mortal Blade \"to sever the ties to immortality\" [5]. This act fulfills Kuro's desire for Immortal Severance while ensuring he does not die permanently, as Wolf \"forsakes his prosthetic arm and the violence it enables\" instead of dying himself [5].": false,
  "12|To obtain the Return ending, you must give Kuro the Frozen Tears and the Divine Dragon's Tears during the ending [2]. Completing this quest line requires obtaining Holy Chapter: Infested, delivering Rice for Kuro to receive Sweet Rice Balls, and exhausting all dialogue with both Kuro and the Divine Child of Rejuvenation [2]. The Divine Heir also grants a gourd of medicinal waters to heal Wolf's wounds if injured [1].": true,
  "13|A Gourd Seed is \"Seed from which healing waters continuously spring forth\" [1]. Giving these seeds to Emma increases the maximum uses of the Healing Gourd, as she explains that \"Adding new seeds will increase the volume of these medicinal waters\" [4].": true,
